# Swashbuckler Extraordinaire: Bot1 attacks with it and chooses to sacrifice no Treasure. Then it did not sacrifice "one
# or more Treasures", and the reflexive ability does not trigger (CR 603.12): no target is asked for, the Treasure
# stays, and the Swashbuckler deals its 2 once. The scenario that sacrifices is the positive control.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Swashbuckler Extraordinaire
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Swashbuckler Extraordinaire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Swashbuckler Extraordinaire > Bot2)
Bot1.Choose()
! Bot1.Target
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Swashbuckler Extraordinaire; Treasure Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Swashbuckler Extraordinaire.Keywords = (absent)
